    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute is over the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee on trip TRP-00202 (Changi Airport Terminal 3, Door 5, night of 24 July 2026). The fee stands as charged, and the driver is paid SGD 4.80. Here is why.\n\nThe platform's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00202, weight 1.0) shows the driver entering the 150 m airport arrival radius at 23:12:45 and holding one unbroken stationary position inside it for 620 seconds, to 23:23:05. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00202, weight 1.0) shows the 'arrived' marker at 23:13:10 and the cancellation at 23:23:20 on reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 are met: the arrival event (a); the in-geofence position at or before it (b); the 480-second minimum hold, exceeded by 140 seconds (c); and termination on a recognised no-show code after the dwell elapsed (d).\n\nNo rider-protective clause displaces that. POL-NS-05 does not fire — at the arrival marker the driver was inside the geofence and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or above, and even recomputed from the first in-geofence fix the dwell still exceeds the minimum. POL-NS-06 does not fire — the effective dwell of 620 seconds is a surplus of 140 seconds against the 480-second airport minimum, not a shortfall. POL-NS-03 does not fire — the driver's closest approach was 22.4 m, inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue. POL-NS-04 does not fire — it requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider during the waiting window, and the chat log holds three messages, one from the system and two from the driver, and none from the rider.\n\nOn the rider's account: I accept that the messages went unread. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00202) is impaired at weight 0.85 on issue UNREAD_MESSAGE, and every message, including the system arrival notice, carries read_at null; trip_record.in_app_calls is empty. That is consistent with the rider's statement that she was in the terminal and saw nothing until later. But it does not move the fee: POL-NS-01 asks whether the driver performed the wait, not whether the rider saw his messages, and POL-NS-04 — the clause that could have turned unanswered contact into a rider win — needs a rider message that was never sent.\n\nOn the rider's whereabouts: the bundle cannot say. All 88 rider fixes report 45–80 m horizontal accuracy, outside the 25 m filter, and are disregarded as evidence of neither presence nor absence; rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0. Under POL-NS-04 and POL-NS-08(b) that limb is undecidable and neutral, and I have treated it as neutral — it is not a finding that the rider was absent. It does not change the outcome, because rider presence is not a condition of POL-NS-01.\n\nThe driver's compensation is 80% of the SGD 6.00 fee, SGD 4.80 (POL-NS-07). The anti-farming check does not trip: 1 no-show termination in 30 days against the threshold of 4, and a rate of 1/168 = 0.006 against 0.08. The driver profile (EV-DPROF-00202) is impaired at weight 0.9 on issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH; the two counters the clause reads sit an order of magnitude below their thresholds, so the discount does not disturb the finding. The SGD 6.00 fee reconciles with the schedule's greater-of rule (AIRPORT zone-class fee SGD 6.00 against the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. There is no false-arrival record to refer, no billing-integrity referral and no anti-farming escalation packet, so the referrals list is empty.\n\nConfidence: the dwell finding rests on EV-GPS-00202 and EV-TRIP-00202, both at weight 1.0; the compensation finding also touches EV-DPROF-00202 at 0.9, so I state confidence at 0.90. That is above the 0.70 escalation floor, so no part of this case is held for review. One open question, for the platform rather than a referral: the driver's messages and the system notice were never marked read, which suggests a notification-delivery gap worth examining — but that does not change this outcome. Ruling: the rider's claim is not supported, the SGD 6.00 charge stands, and the driver receives SGD 4.80."
  },
